 Function           What it does                           Example                                       
JSON_OBJECT()   | Creates a JSON object                   JSON_OBJECT('name','John','age',25)       
 JSON_ARRAY()    | Creates a JSON array                    JSON_ARRAY('Python','SQL','Java')           
 JSON_EXTRACT()  | Gets data from JSON                     JSON_EXTRACT(data, '$.name')                
 ->              | Shortcut for JSON extraction            data->'$.name                              
 ->>             | Extracts JSON value as plain text       data->>'$.name                             
 JSON_SET()      | Adds/updates a value                    JSON_SET(data, '$.age', 26)                 
 JSON_REPLACE()  | Updates existing value                  JSON_REPLACE(data, '$.age', 26)             
 JSON_REMOVE()   | Removes a JSON value                    JSON_REMOVE(data, '$.age')                  
 JSON_CONTAINS() | Checks whether JSON contains something  JSON_CONTAINS(data, '"Python"', '$.skills') 
 JSON_VALID()    | Checks whether JSON is valid            JSON_VALID(data)                            

One example to understand the whole concept
-- Suppose data Stored in a column profile
{
  "name": "Paramesh",
  "age": 23,
  "skills": ["Python", "SQL"]
}

-- Get name
SELECT profile->>'$.name';

-- Get age
SELECT profile->>'$.age';

-- Get skills
SELECT profile->'$.skills';

-- Update age
SELECT JSON_SET(profile, '$.age', 24);

-- Remove age
SELECT JSON_REMOVE(profile, '$.age');

-- Check whether Python exists
SELECT JSON_CONTAINS(profile, '"Python"', '$.skills');


